---
import BlogLayout from "../../layouts/BlogLayout.astro";

const title = "Hong Kong Car Tax Guide: First Registration Tax (FRT) & Licensing";
const description = "Complete guide to Hong Kong car tax, First Registration Tax (FRT) tier rates, annual motor vehicle licensing fees, electric vehicle (EV) tax concessions, and calculation.";
const image = "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1554224154-26032ffc0d07?w=1200&q=80";
const canonical = "https://finsiva.com/blogs/hong-kong-car-tax-guide";

const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How is First Registration Tax (FRT) calculated in Hong Kong?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "First Registration Tax (FRT) for private cars is calculated on a progressive tier system based on the taxable value of the vehicle: 46% on the first HK$150,000, 72% on the next HK$150,000, 100% on the next HK$200,000, and 115% on the remainder over HK$500,000."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Are electric vehicles (EVs) exempt from First Registration Tax in Hong Kong?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Under the EV concession scheme, private electric cars enjoy an FRT tax concession capped at HK$58,500. Under the 'One-for-One Replacement' Scheme (scrapping an eligible old private car), eligible buyers receive an increased FRT concession cap of up to HK$172,500."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the annual motor vehicle license fee in Hong Kong?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Annual vehicle licensing fees (Motor Vehicle Tax) for petrol private cars are determined by engine capacity (CC): HK$5,074 for ≤1,500cc, HK$7,019 for 1,501–2,500cc, HK$8,964 for 2,501–3,500cc, HK$10,910 for 3,501–4,500cc, and HK$12,855 for >4,500cc."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do I pay First Registration Tax on imported used cars?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Imported used cars must undergo valuation by the Transport Department to establish their taxable value in Hong Kong before FRT is levied at standard tier rates."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---

<BlogLayout title={title} description={description} image={image} canonical={canonical} author="David Chan" authorBio="David Chan is a transport duty specialist covering Hong Kong First Registration Tax, vehicle licensing, and Transport Department regulations." lastUpdated="August 2026" readTime="10 min read">
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

  <div class="min-h-screen bg-canvas dark:bg-canvas">
    <main class="min-h-screen">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-6 text-sm">
          <ol class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><a href="/" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Home</a></li>
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="text-muted">/</span><a href="/blogs" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Blogs</a></li>
            <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="text-muted">/</span><span class="font-medium text-ink dark:text-on-primary" aria-current="page">Hong Kong Car Tax Guide</span></li>
          </ol>
        </nav>

        <article class="prose max-w-none">
          <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-ink mb-4 dark:text-on-primary">Hong Kong Car Tax Guide: First Registration Tax & Motor Vehicle Licensing</h1>
          <p class="text-lg text-body dark:text-muted">Last updated: August 2026 | Verified Transport Department Rules | 10 min read</p>

          <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1554224154-26032ffc0d07?w=1200&q=80" alt="Hong Kong vehicle traffic and city skyline - Car Tax Guide" class="mb-6 w-full rounded-lg object-cover max-h-80 sm:max-h-96" loading="lazy" />

          <!-- Early Calculator CTA -->
          <div class="my-6 p-6 rounded-2xl border border-primary/30 bg-primary/5 dark:border-primary/20 dark:bg-primary/5 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Calculate Your HK First Registration Tax (FRT)</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-body dark:text-muted mt-1">Estimate FRT progressive tiers, EV concessions, and total vehicle registration costs instantly.</p>
            </div>
            <a href="/countries/hong-kong/stamp-duty/first-registration-tax-calculator" class="btn btn-primary text-sm font-semibold shrink-0 px-5 py-2.5">
              Launch FRT Car Tax Calculator →
            </a>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-body dark:text-muted leading-relaxed">
            <p>Vehicle ownership in Hong Kong involves substantial upfront duties and ongoing licensing fees designed to manage road traffic density. The primary car taxes administered by the <strong>Transport Department</strong> under the <em>Motor Vehicles (First Registration Tax) Ordinance (Cap. 330)</em> are <strong>First Registration Tax (FRT)</strong> and annual <strong>Vehicle License Fees</strong>.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">First Registration Tax (FRT) Progressive Rates</h2>
            <p>First Registration Tax is a one-off tax levied on private cars when first registered in Hong Kong. The tax is calculated progressively on the taxable value (published retail price or assessed import value):</p>

            <div class="my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
              <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
                <thead class="bg-canvas-soft border-b border-hairline dark:bg-surface/80 dark:border-overlay-lighter text-ink dark:text-on-primary font-bold">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="p-3">Taxable Value Bracket (HKD)</th>
                    <th class="p-3">FRT Rate</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody class="divide-y divide-hairline dark:divide-overlay-lighter">
                  <tr><td class="p-3">First HK$150,000</td><td class="p-3 font-bold text-primary dark:text-on-primary">46%</td></tr>
                  <tr><td class="p-3">Next HK$150,000 (HK$150,001 – HK$300,000)</td><td class="p-3 font-bold text-primary dark:text-on-primary">72%</td></tr>
                  <tr><td class="p-3">Next HK$200,000 (HK$300,001 – HK$500,000)</td><td class="p-3 font-bold text-primary dark:text-on-primary">100%</td></tr>
                  <tr><td class="p-3">Remainder (Above HK$500,000)</td><td class="p-3 font-bold text-primary dark:text-on-primary">115%</td></tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Electric Vehicle (EV) Concessions & One-for-One Scheme</h2>
            <p>To promote clean transportation, the Hong Kong Government provides First Registration Tax concessions for Electric Vehicles (EVs):</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
              <li><strong>Standard EV Concession:</strong> Private electric cars receive an FRT tax concession cap of up to <strong>HK$58,500</strong>.</li>
              <li><strong>"One-for-One Replacement" Scheme:</strong> Owners who scrap and deregister an eligible old private car to replace it with a new electric car receive an enhanced FRT concession cap of up to <strong>HK$172,500</strong>.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Annual Motor Vehicle Licensing Fees (MVT)</h2>
            <p>Annual vehicle license renewal fees for petrol private passenger cars are determined by engine cylinder capacity (CC):</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 font-mono text-sm">
              <li>Engine Capacity ≤ 1,500cc: HK$5,074 / year</li>
              <li>1,501cc – 2,500cc: HK$7,019 / year</li>
              <li>2,501cc – 3,500cc: HK$8,964 / year</li>
              <li>3,501cc – 4,500cc: HK$10,910 / year</li>
              <li>Above 4,500cc: HK$12,855 / year</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Transport Department Registration Procedures</h2>
            <p>Vehicle buyers must submit registration documents, proof of third-party insurance, vehicle inspection certificates (for vehicles aged 6+ years), and payment of FRT and license fees to the Transport Department licensing office.</p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
            {faqSchema.mainEntity.map(faq => (
              <div class="my-4 p-4 rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">{faq.name}</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-body dark:text-muted mt-1 leading-relaxed">{faq.acceptedAnswer.text}</p>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>

          <!-- Internal Resource Linking Grid -->
          <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-hairline dark:border-overlay-lighter">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mb-6 dark:text-on-primary">Hong Kong Tax Tools & Related Guides</h2>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
              <a href="/countries/hong-kong/stamp-duty/first-registration-tax-calculator" class="block rounded-xl border border-hairline p-4 hover:border-primary transition bg-canvas dark:bg-surface dark:border-overlay-lighter">
                <h3 class="font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary text-sm">HK FRT Car Tax Calculator</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-1">Calculate FRT progressive tiers & EV concessions.</p>
              </a>
              <a href="/blogs/hong-kong-stamp-duty-guide" class="block rounded-xl border border-hairline p-4 hover:border-primary transition bg-canvas dark:bg-surface dark:border-overlay-lighter">
                <h3 class="font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary text-sm">Hong Kong Stamp Duty Guide</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-1">Property conveyancing & lease stamping.</p>
              </a>
              <a href="/blogs/hong-kong-property-tax-guide" class="block rounded-xl border border-hairline p-4 hover:border-primary transition bg-canvas dark:bg-surface dark:border-overlay-lighter">
                <h3 class="font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary text-sm">Hong Kong Property Tax Guide</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-1">15% standard rate on rental income.</p>
              </a>
              <a href="/blogs/hong-kong-salaries-tax-guide" class="block rounded-xl border border-hairline p-4 hover:border-primary transition bg-canvas dark:bg-surface dark:border-overlay-lighter">
                <h3 class="font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary text-sm">Hong Kong Salaries Tax Guide</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-1">Income tax brackets (2%-17%) & MPF rules.</p>
              </a>
              <a href="/blogs/hong-kong-etax-guide" class="block rounded-xl border border-hairline p-4 hover:border-primary transition bg-canvas dark:bg-surface dark:border-overlay-lighter">
                <h3 class="font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary text-sm">Hong Kong eTAX Guide</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-1">File tax returns online via IRD portal.</p>
              </a>
              <a href="/blogs/hong-kong-tax-allowances-deductions" class="block rounded-xl border border-hairline p-4 hover:border-primary transition bg-canvas dark:bg-surface dark:border-overlay-lighter">
                <h3 class="font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary text-sm">Tax Allowances & Deductions</h3>
                <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-1">Personal allowances & MPF deductions.</p>
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink mt-12 mb-6 dark:text-on-primary">Official Authorities & References</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-body dark:text-muted">
            <li><a href="https://www.td.gov.hk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Transport Department - First Registration Tax & Licensing</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://www.epd.gov.hk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Environmental Protection Department - EV Concession Scheme</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://www.gov.hk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Hong Kong Government Official Portal</a></li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>
</BlogLayout>
